    "created_at": "2016-01-20T16:16:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-20T16:20:17Z",
    "body": "Read my example again. When you call \"set the url\" from that clause, it will fail to parse the URL, since relative URLs parsed relative to invalid bases fail to parse. So it will start null, per \"If resolving was aborted with an error, set this element's url to null.\".\n\nAnd when I go to change the base href, that does not cause that clause to trigger. The only time to do an update is upon doing a subsequent setter or getter.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
